{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VUfNMocvpSc81wRL5kv4ba","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu API workout_doc hr target units %lthr start end format\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129\"},{\"title\":\"HR target workouts broken on Edge 840 firmware ≥30.18 — interpreted as %HRmax instead of bpm\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20\"},{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu Claude AI Athlete Training Automation n8n\",\"url\":\"https://growwstacks.com/workflows/convert-training-prescriptions-to-intervalsicu-workouts-with-claude-opus-ai\"},{\"title\":\"forum.intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=19\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Cycling Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md\"},{\"title\":\"9822 convert training prescriptions to intervalsicu workouts with claude opus ai\",\"url\":\"https://n8n.io/workflows/9822-convert-training-prescriptions-to-intervalsicu-workouts-with-claude-opus-ai/\"}]\n\nThe search turned up forum threads and third-party docs, but no official schema that confirms the exact `%lthr` unit string or the start/end field layout for HR steps.\n\n- **Units:** One developer noted that HR-based workout editing supported only %HR at the time, not absolute HR, and that LTHR and max HR weren't included in the JSON ([forum thread, page 129](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129)). The maintainer later added `lthr`, `max_hr`, `threshold_pace` and `pace_units` fields ([same thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129)). I didn't find a `%lthr` unit string in the results.\n- **Step format:** A power step looks like `\"power\": {\"value\": 43, \"units\": \"%ftp\"}` with a duration in seconds ([forum thread, page 7](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7)). An HR bug report cites an HR-zone variant, `hr: {units: \"hr_zone\", value: 2}`, which the author says gets stripped on export ([Edge 840 bug report](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090)).\n- **Resolved start/end:** Resolved steps carry underscore-prefixed `_power` objects with `start` and `end` values in absolute terms, and these can appear even when the step has no range ([forum thread, page 20](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20)).\n- **Default HR range:** When fixed targets are expanded into ranges, the default HR spread is 1.5%, and the `hrRange` query parameter can override it ([forum thread, post 389](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389)).\n\nFor the authoritative `hr` schema, check the intervals.icu API docs or inspect a JSON download of an HR workout from your own account. The download endpoint is `/api/v1/athlete/{id}/events/{eventId}/download{ext}` ([forum thread, post 129](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129)).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6543445-6ad1-4b9e-8dc7-218bf60ae8fb","uuid":"c74631c9-408d-4fac-a2cf-aee0ace1a739","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:25:41.415Z","tool_use_re