{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS7CNzXppXSaQinihjqH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed the generator to write HR corridors with `start` instead of `value` as the lower bound. I could not confirm the fix against the watch or the Intervals.icu schema, so it still needs a live check.\n\n**The change:** in `gen.py`, `hr_target()` now returns `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. I regenerated `plans/tempo-run.json` locally. Every HR step now carries a proper range, including the repeated Tempo and Float steps. I changed nothing else, and nothing was pushed.\n\n**Why I think this is the cause:** the generator used `value` as the lower bound, and the Intervals.icu power example uses `value` for a single target. A range is probably expected under `start`. If `value` is read as a single point, Intervals exports one target and the watch snaps it to its nearest zone band, which matches the readback. The web search did not confirm the official schema, so this is an inference.\n\n**Ruled out by the readback:** the units are not the problem, since `bpm` gave 214–249 bpm. The `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` keys are not the fix either, since they gave a constant 101.\n\n**To verify:** push the regenerated event with `./push.sh event.json`, then check that the HR targets come back with `start`/`end` and that the watch shows 117–129, 151–160, 129–141 and 112–124 after re-sync. If the watch still shows zone bands, check whether Intervals exports HR as zone targets for this athlete. ANSWER.md has the details.\n\nI wrote `ANSWER.md` in the repo. I briefly wrote a scratch file to `/tmp`, outside the working directory, and deleted it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":552,"cache_read_input_tokens":29614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":552},"output_toke